WEBVTT

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:15.420
Who cares about this Princess of Mai High crap?

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:17.610
I'm skipping the after-party.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:21.040
I want to get this stupid outfit off right now.

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:23.480
Oh, you're right. It's open.

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:24.250
But...

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:25.500
<b>Festival Eve Dressing Rooms</b>

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:26.560
Do you think we can actually get on the roof?

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:30.750
It's okay, I know the passcode for the door.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.380
How do you know that?

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:33.880
Because I go to the roof all the time.

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:35.320
Typical gamer.

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:36.840
I don't see how that's relevant.

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:41.910
Looks like they're getting along just fine.

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:18.180
Wow, this is a nice spot.

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:21.200
No one's around, and it's cold.

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:25.510
And the campfire looks like a little speck.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.730
Are you mocking me?

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:36.910
Oh, Katsuragi!

00:02:36.910 --> 00:02:38.050
I can see the Akanemaru!

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:45.710
Okay, maybe not...

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:53.240
Say something...

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:56.190
This feels weird.

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:59.270
You're not acting like your usual self.

00:02:59.270 --> 00:03:00.700
How so?

00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:03.200
You're throwing me off.

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:07.500
It's just as weird for me.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:10.910
I never thought I'd be talking to you this way.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:17.690
Before, my walking around with a geek like you

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:19.130
would have been absurd.

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:24.650
But today, I feel like I want to always

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:27.140
be with you.

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:32.190
W-Well, "always" may be an overstatement...

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:40.440
Um...

00:03:41.710 --> 00:03:42.930
Katsuragi...

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:47.710
Ka—

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:50.200
Ch-Chihiro!

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:00.050
Chihiro, c-can I?

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:03.470
Uh-huh...

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:07.430
Katsuragi, be gentle...

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:10.810
This is

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:15.060
my first time.

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:16.070
Huh?

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:22.040
This is

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:23.990
your first kiss?

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:25.910
Yes...

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:28.240
Is that bad?

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:32.940
No, it isn't.

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:37.780
<i>There's no way she'd lie in this situation.</i>

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:41.760
<i>She's telling the truth...</i>

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:45.130
<i>Chihiro doesn't remember the conquest...</i>

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:49.060
<i>There is no goddess inside</i>

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:52.440
<i>Chihiro...</i>

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:56.650
<b>Girls Dressing Room</b>

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:06.620
Ayumi.

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:09.410
Don't cry, Ayumi.

00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:12.020
I'm not crying...

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:17.510
<i>I can confirm she's not hosting 
a goddess before the ending.</i>

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:21.170
<i>This was the last chance.</i>

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:22.920
<i>I can still turn back.</i>

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:25.920
What's wrong?

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:29.370
<i>I can end Chihiro's conquest,</i>

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:31.000
<i>then switch over to Ayumi's route.</i>

00:05:31.660 --> 00:05:34.600
<i>I just have to say, "You seem to be confused.</i>

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.940
<i>I brought you here to ask how 
I can get closer to Ayumi."</i>

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:39.930
<i>That will result in the target and 
accomplice switching places.</i>

00:05:39.930 --> 00:05:41.730
<i>A Copernican revolution.</i>

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:42.440
<i>There will be some...</i>

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:44.770
<i>No, a lot of trouble...</i>

00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:46.200
<i>But I can handle it.</i>

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:48.950
Chihiro.

00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:51.080
Huh? Eh?

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:52.990
Wh-What?

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:55.770
<i>Wait...</i>

00:05:57.190 --> 00:06:00.710
<i>Is that the right thing to say?</i>

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:06.090
<i>Thinking back, Chihiro always acted 
before I could do anything myself.</i>

00:06:06.710 --> 00:06:09.680
<i>I only appeared to be going down her route.</i>

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:11.520
<i>It didn't have anything to do with conquest.</i>

00:06:12.110 --> 00:06:14.850
<i>So how do I explain the current situation?</i>

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:20.510
Katsuragi?

00:06:22.370 --> 00:06:23.560
Chihiro...

00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:26.110
Do you really love me?

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:30.690
Wh-Why would you ask that?

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:35.790
Yes, I do.

00:06:36.890 --> 00:06:37.860
Why?

00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:38.790
Since when?

00:06:39.610 --> 00:06:41.620
Since when did you feel that way?

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:43.110
Since when...?

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:46.370
I-It's hard to say,

00:06:46.370 --> 00:06:47.630
but I guess sometime in the spring.

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:49.450
What?

00:06:50.290 --> 00:06:53.070
I'd understand that if you still 
remembered the conquest,

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:55.330
but I didn't even interact with you in spring!

00:06:55.900 --> 00:06:57.940
What do you mean, "conquest"?

00:06:57.940 --> 00:06:59.070
I m-mean...

00:06:59.070 --> 00:07:01.080
You were always making fun of me,

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:03.130
and you asked out a bunch of different guys!

00:07:03.130 --> 00:07:05.590
Ah! That's not important!

00:07:05.590 --> 00:07:06.970
But...

00:07:06.970 --> 00:07:08.240
You...

00:07:08.620 --> 00:07:10.800
You were the one

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:12.990
I was always thinking about!

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:21.590
Tomorrow is the Mai High Festival!

00:07:21.590 --> 00:07:25.040
Let's have the time of our lives!

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:34.010
I-It's impossible to fall in love 
with someone that way.

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:37.070
There was no conquest, no interaction...

00:07:37.070 --> 00:07:39.060
What would make you fall in love with me?

00:07:40.260 --> 00:07:43.270
You don't need a reason to fall in love.

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:54.660
I just realized at some point that I loved you!

00:08:13.150 --> 00:08:14.490
Katsuragi...

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:17.970
Do you love me?

00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:25.940
Of course not.

00:08:26.920 --> 00:08:27.690
Huh?

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:30.110
Katsuragi?

00:08:32.970 --> 00:08:35.450
This is stupid. I'm leaving.

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:40.200
You actually thought I'd fall 
in love with a real girl?

00:08:41.980 --> 00:08:42.730
What?

00:08:43.420 --> 00:08:47.460
Then why did you go on 
a date with me today?

00:08:48.430 --> 00:08:50.020
This doesn't count as a date.

00:08:53.070 --> 00:08:55.270
I was just pulling one over on a real girl.

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:56.590
Stupid.

00:09:03.490 --> 00:09:04.400
You're lying...

00:09:05.950 --> 00:09:07.180
You must be lying...

00:09:16.150 --> 00:09:18.710
You've always made fun of me,

00:09:18.710 --> 00:09:20.370
so I wanted some payback.

00:09:20.890 --> 00:09:22.790
But I've had enough.

00:09:23.610 --> 00:09:25.370
Stay away from me.

00:09:26.230 --> 00:09:27.180
Ka—

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:01.280
Katsuragi...

00:10:01.900 --> 00:10:05.040
Why did you say that?

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:07.290
Ayumi! Why are you here?

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:11.540
I thought you went out with Chihiro 
because you knew how she felt.

00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:13.920
How could you say those things?

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:19.430
I r-realized that...

00:10:20.290 --> 00:10:23.520
I've been lying to myself.

00:10:24.230 --> 00:10:26.390
But now I know

00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:30.520
who I truly care about...

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:34.020
It's...

00:10:38.960 --> 00:10:41.920
You're a total jerk!

00:10:43.940 --> 00:10:45.730
A total jerk...

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:53.400
Yes...

00:10:54.970 --> 00:10:56.340
I am.

00:11:02.130 --> 00:11:05.850
Ayumi, why did you go to the roof?

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:08.430
This is your own fault.

00:11:08.980 --> 00:11:12.440
Why mope over a man you've given up on?

00:11:12.760 --> 00:11:15.640
Humans are so inefficient.

00:11:30.630 --> 00:11:31.720
Katsuragi...

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:35.220
Diana?

00:11:35.660 --> 00:11:36.960
Why are you here?

00:11:37.510 --> 00:11:40.240
Is your search going well?

00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:43.390
It is. No problems at all.

00:11:44.290 --> 00:11:46.120
There's only one goddess left.

00:11:46.780 --> 00:11:48.250
That'll be the end of it.

00:11:48.760 --> 00:11:49.860
No.

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:51.390
There are two left.

00:11:55.330 --> 00:11:59.610
P-Please bring out my wings, too...

00:12:00.600 --> 00:12:02.860
I have something to tell you.

00:12:03.560 --> 00:12:05.080
It appears that

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:07.620
I've fallen in love with you!

00:12:08.690 --> 00:12:09.670
Huh?

00:12:09.670 --> 00:12:12.000
Ah, so...

00:12:12.670 --> 00:12:17.500
I realize that falling in love with 
Tenri's fiancé is inexcusable.

00:12:17.910 --> 00:12:20.600
I believe my wings have not returned

00:12:20.600 --> 00:12:26.510
because my guilt is curtailing 
the power of Tenri's love.

00:12:27.370 --> 00:12:30.270
There's no time to waste.

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:32.750
Please love Tenri.

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:36.310
Before I fall deeper in love with you!

00:12:52.130 --> 00:12:53.030
Tenri!

00:12:53.030 --> 00:12:54.390
I did all this for—

00:12:55.260 --> 00:12:57.380
Stay away, you animal!

00:13:00.730 --> 00:13:03.420
Keima! Why am I here?

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:04.800
Would you calm down?

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:06.050
Now, Tenri...

00:13:06.250 --> 00:13:08.140
Tell him how you feel!

00:13:08.140 --> 00:13:10.810
Or my wings will never return!

00:13:11.120 --> 00:13:13.600
I-It isn't that simple...

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:15.560
This is all your fault!

00:13:15.810 --> 00:13:20.680
You're such a hermit, I'm always 
the one who has to talk to him.

00:13:20.680 --> 00:13:25.190
I had no previous experience talking to men.

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:28.240
So after spending all this time with him,

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:31.920
it's natural that I'd fall in love, 
even with a lowlife like him!

00:13:31.920 --> 00:13:33.330
The hell kind of logic is that?

00:13:33.650 --> 00:13:35.260
You're not normal, Tenri.

00:13:35.260 --> 00:13:36.040
Huh?

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:38.710
You live next door to someone 
you've loved for ten years...

00:13:38.950 --> 00:13:43.090
You must want to talk to him, 
to spend more time with him!

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:45.470
Not that I have those urges.

00:13:45.830 --> 00:13:48.760
You should tell him how you truly feel, Tenri!

00:13:53.780 --> 00:13:55.430
What do you want to do, Tenri?

00:13:55.950 --> 00:13:56.560
Huh?

00:13:57.050 --> 00:14:00.370
I'm sick of cryptic conversations!

00:14:01.140 --> 00:14:03.820
There's a proper sequence 
that should be followed!

00:14:04.220 --> 00:14:07.170
But you all just keep adding more useless noise!

00:14:07.590 --> 00:14:09.320
Seriously, what...

00:14:13.750 --> 00:14:16.350
What... am I doing?

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:18.410
Keima...

00:14:18.770 --> 00:14:20.170
Did something happen?

00:14:20.740 --> 00:14:21.590
Nothing happened.

00:14:22.470 --> 00:14:23.540
Just leave.

00:14:48.080 --> 00:14:49.030
Tenri?

00:14:49.690 --> 00:14:50.740
Keima...

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:53.370
Did you say something?

00:14:56.840 --> 00:14:58.510
It's a fake ear.

00:14:58.510 --> 00:15:00.300
Yeah, I can see that...

00:15:00.300 --> 00:15:01.630
Why are you performing magic tricks?

00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:05.210
You looked like you were feeling down,

00:15:05.210 --> 00:15:07.380
so I wanted to make you smile...

00:15:08.010 --> 00:15:09.260
I don't feel down.

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:11.140
I'm perfectly normal.

00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:14.160
I can also do escape tricks.

00:15:14.160 --> 00:15:15.030
That's big.

00:15:15.030 --> 00:15:16.900
You really like magic, huh?

00:15:17.860 --> 00:15:19.490
Please lock the box.

00:15:19.490 --> 00:15:20.820
Why me?

00:15:23.250 --> 00:15:26.820
I do love you, Keima.

00:15:27.810 --> 00:15:32.570
But the Keima I love is the one 
who's always playing games.

00:15:33.390 --> 00:15:37.150
I want you to go back to your normal self,

00:15:37.150 --> 00:15:40.330
and smile all the time.

00:15:40.900 --> 00:15:44.020
You don't have to worry about me.

00:15:44.020 --> 00:15:46.840
I'll find a way to bring Diana's wings back.

00:15:47.410 --> 00:15:48.450
How?

00:15:49.060 --> 00:15:50.380
I'm not sure...

00:15:52.230 --> 00:15:56.600
No one will do what I want them to.

00:15:57.740 --> 00:15:59.600
But you have my thanks.

00:16:00.250 --> 00:16:03.850
Um, you don't have to force yourself to smile.

00:16:05.600 --> 00:16:06.970
Yeah...

00:16:07.550 --> 00:16:09.860
But I have to keep going, 
or this will never end.

00:16:11.610 --> 00:16:13.810
Is there any more to your magic show?

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:16.990
Might as well see what else you can do.

00:16:16.990 --> 00:16:20.180
Then I'll use this magic wand...

00:16:20.180 --> 00:16:22.480
Is this the one where flowers 
pop out of the wand?

00:16:22.480 --> 00:16:26.030
W-Well, I already did my best trick...

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:31.130
<b>Mai High Festival</b>

00:16:28.400 --> 00:16:31.130
<b>Mai High Festival, Day 1</b>

00:16:31.130 --> 00:16:33.630
<b>3 Hours Before the Festival</b>

00:16:46.910 --> 00:16:47.820
Elsie?

00:16:47.820 --> 00:16:49.190
Exalted Brother!

00:16:50.160 --> 00:16:53.020
Our band's having a dress rehearsal.

00:16:53.020 --> 00:16:54.860
Are you here to listen to us?

00:16:55.310 --> 00:16:56.880
Er, wait...

00:16:56.880 --> 00:16:58.870
No one else is here yet.

00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:00.820
<i>Dress rehearsal?</i>

00:17:01.780 --> 00:17:05.370
Gawd, and here I'm so busy being a celeb...

00:17:05.890 --> 00:17:08.660
I've gotta book it to another 
rehearsal right after this,

00:17:08.660 --> 00:17:11.550
and I <i>totes</i> have no time to reschedule.

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:13.880
Talk like a normal person.

00:17:16.250 --> 00:17:18.060
<i>The concert is tomorrow.</i>

00:17:18.490 --> 00:17:21.080
<i>Should I attempt to conquer Ayumi now?</i>

00:17:22.050 --> 00:17:23.930
Did you know, Exalted Brother...

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:26.900
That the Mai High Festival has 
been around for a long time?

00:17:27.420 --> 00:17:29.410
Nikaido mentioned something about it.

00:17:29.410 --> 00:17:31.390
Hasn't it been around since 
the school was founded?

00:17:31.390 --> 00:17:32.610
Wrong!

00:17:33.180 --> 00:17:36.030
The festival was around before our school.

00:17:36.370 --> 00:17:38.780
Oh... It's that old?

00:17:40.930 --> 00:17:44.790
I never really noticed, but our school emblem is...

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:46.290
School emblem?

00:17:47.330 --> 00:17:48.380
A goddess...

00:17:52.830 --> 00:17:55.030
What's wrong, Exalted Brother?

00:17:55.030 --> 00:17:56.800
Why did we come to the theater?

00:17:57.230 --> 00:17:59.470
<i>This is the oldest building around.</i>

00:18:00.100 --> 00:18:03.830
<i>Ten years ago, we found a swarm 
of loose souls underneath.</i>

00:18:04.740 --> 00:18:06.910
<i>The goddesses... Maijima...</i>

00:18:07.370 --> 00:18:10.810
<i>I have the feeling that everything is connected.</i>

00:18:13.170 --> 00:18:13.820
Huh?

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:15.740
What's wrong?

00:18:16.020 --> 00:18:17.910
The hole's gone...

00:18:19.080 --> 00:18:23.120
When I came here with Tenri during 
summer break, there was a hole.

00:18:24.590 --> 00:18:25.420
Elsie...

00:18:25.420 --> 00:18:26.250
Huh?

00:18:26.430 --> 00:18:27.560
Let's move.

00:18:27.560 --> 00:18:29.500
What? Right now?

00:18:29.810 --> 00:18:30.910
It won't take long.

00:18:30.910 --> 00:18:31.750
Ten minutes.

00:18:32.820 --> 00:18:35.500
<b>Maijima Seaside Park, Artificial Beach</b>

00:18:36.830 --> 00:18:38.260
The exit's gone, too...

00:18:39.080 --> 00:18:42.200
That hole couldn't have disappeared naturally.

00:18:42.200 --> 00:18:43.470
Someone must have sealed it off.

00:18:47.590 --> 00:18:48.460
Elsie.

00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:50.520
Let's go over there.

00:18:51.400 --> 00:18:53.070
You mean that rock?

00:18:53.070 --> 00:18:56.280
Yeah, use your raiment to make us invisible.

00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:57.240
Huh?

00:18:58.270 --> 00:19:00.330
Why do we need to be invisible?

00:19:00.330 --> 00:19:01.490
Just a precaution.

00:19:01.930 --> 00:19:03.980
That's a big rock.

00:19:03.980 --> 00:19:05.970
It's known as Point Rock.

00:19:05.970 --> 00:19:07.450
People usually stay away.

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:08.910
Let's check the other side.

00:19:11.970 --> 00:19:13.900
I don't see anything.

00:19:13.900 --> 00:19:15.650
No, look down there.

00:19:16.770 --> 00:19:18.660
The waves don't look right.

00:19:18.660 --> 00:19:20.120
Let's check below.

00:19:20.650 --> 00:19:22.200
Underwater?

00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:24.000
Yes, hurry up.

00:19:25.250 --> 00:19:28.050
My clothes will get wet!

00:19:34.930 --> 00:19:35.780
Huh?

00:19:35.780 --> 00:19:38.490
We went through the rock...

00:19:41.480 --> 00:19:43.240
Just like ten years ago.

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:45.740
There's an opening under the water.

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:49.800
<i>Still, getting in was too easy.</i>

00:19:49.800 --> 00:19:51.140
<i>Did I guess wrong?</i>

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:14.400
E-Exalted Brother, this is...

00:20:14.910 --> 00:20:16.900
Elsie, time to run.

00:20:25.360 --> 00:20:26.410
Exalted Brother!

00:20:26.410 --> 00:20:28.320
Don't stop! Get us out 
of here as fast as you can!

00:20:28.320 --> 00:20:29.370
Hurry up!

00:20:29.370 --> 00:20:31.180
O-Okay!

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:36.120
Why did you remove the barrier?

00:20:36.530 --> 00:20:39.660
It wouldn't do for them to 
be trapped by the barrier.

00:20:39.660 --> 00:20:42.000
If they're captured, 
we'll be at a disadvantage.

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:44.060
And it appears that they weren't seen.

00:20:44.530 --> 00:20:47.310
The ones that are inside wouldn't 
have noticed the opening.

00:20:47.310 --> 00:20:49.470
My obliteration of the barrier was flawless.

00:20:49.910 --> 00:20:53.850
I'll check to make sure they weren't bugged.

00:20:53.850 --> 00:20:55.440
You worry too much.

00:20:56.060 --> 00:20:59.980
That's what being a homeroom teacher means.

00:21:01.540 --> 00:21:03.720
No tracers or anything on me, right?

00:21:03.720 --> 00:21:04.970
Nope.

00:21:04.970 --> 00:21:08.990
But I can't believe there was 
a place like that inside the rock.

00:21:09.540 --> 00:21:11.490
What was that place?

00:21:11.490 --> 00:21:13.120
It certainly looked ominous...

00:21:13.280 --> 00:21:17.380
The egg-like things lying around looked familiar.

00:21:17.630 --> 00:21:20.290
Those were mature loose souls!

00:21:20.290 --> 00:21:23.230
And the black figures belonged to Vintage!

00:21:23.230 --> 00:21:26.930
Vintage is raising loose souls so 
they can revive the Weiss!

00:21:27.300 --> 00:21:29.490
Raising loose souls? Without hosts?

00:21:29.490 --> 00:21:30.940
Um... Um...

00:21:30.940 --> 00:21:35.560
Elsie, do you know why our 
school emblem is a hexagon?

00:21:36.520 --> 00:21:37.190
Huh?

00:21:37.590 --> 00:21:39.020
The goddess on our school emblem...

00:21:39.480 --> 00:21:40.770
The swarm of loose souls...

00:21:41.090 --> 00:21:42.650
The underground passage that was sealed...

00:21:43.500 --> 00:21:45.060
The operation being run beneath the rock...

00:21:46.050 --> 00:21:50.510
Something huge is about to happen here.

00:21:51.990 --> 00:21:53.040
In other words...

00:21:54.570 --> 00:21:56.540
It has nothing to do with me.

00:21:57.090 --> 00:21:59.710
Man, I wasted all that time on an empty route.

00:21:59.710 --> 00:22:00.840
What?

00:22:00.840 --> 00:22:04.220
Aren't you going to do anything 
with that information?

00:22:04.600 --> 00:22:08.550
If those loose souls are released, 
terrible things will happen!

00:22:08.550 --> 00:22:10.340
So you can end it then, right?

00:22:12.240 --> 00:22:16.040
Whatever happens, all I have to 
do is proceed with the conquest.

00:22:24.760 --> 00:22:26.700
We're approaching ten o'clock!

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:29.200
The festival will soon open to the public!

00:22:29.950 --> 00:22:33.170
The Mai High Festival's about to begin!

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:20.460
<b>Labyrinth</b>

00:24:06.010 --> 00:24:09.600
I've played games in which the 
last boss appears as the first enemy.

00:24:09.600 --> 00:24:11.470
But I didn't expect Ayumi 
to host the last goddess.

00:24:11.470 --> 00:24:13.930
And Vintage is getting aggressive.

00:24:13.930 --> 00:24:15.430
Time to go on the offensive, Elsie!

00:24:15.430 --> 00:24:16.570
Sorry!

00:24:16.570 --> 00:24:19.200
All requests must go through 
my agency and manager.
